From eb30c8dce6e9a7ad07335a3f645f9b8298f95bb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:50:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] Round 8: Pool domain scratch buffers across calls

Prepared keeps a mutex-protected pool of at most 64 scratch sets. The
inline caller and each worker take one per batch and return it, so
consecutive single-candidate calls reuse warm buffers. A test compares
pooled results with fresh evaluators across models, budgets, worker
counts and traced records, and checks the pool limit.

Workload: one in matrix mode (one candidate per call), 11 samples.
Before median: 0.731 us. After median: 0.496 us. Speedup: 1.47x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
